## 11. Troubleshooting

### 11.1 Common Issues

| Issue | Solution |
|----|----|
| Recognition not working | Verify XPath expression with message samples |
| JAXB generation fails | Check XSD validity and package configuration |
| Validation errors not clear | Add detailed error messages to validators |
| Transformation fails | Check null handling and field mappings |
| Unrecognized messages | Review recognition rules and test coverage |

### 11.2 Validation Checklist

- [ ] Schema files are in correct location
- [ ] JAXB POJOs generated successfully
- [ ] Recognition rules tested with sample messages
- [ ] Each validation rule has separate validator
- [ ] Validators registered as Spring components
- [ ] Metadata extractors configured correctly
- [ ] Transformers only contain transformation logic
- [ ] Target JSON structure defined
- [ ] Integration tests cover all phases
- [ ] Error handling tested

### 11.3 Performance Optimization

- Use specific XPath expressions to reduce processing
- Generate JAXB POJOs once, not on every build
- Cache metadata extraction results when appropriate
- Optimize transformation logic for large messages
- Use appropriate logging levels

### 11.4 Debugging Tips

1. Enable DEBUG logging for specific packages
2. Verify message content at each phase boundary
3. Test validators independently with unit tests
4. Validate XSD schema separately
5. Check JAXB deserialization with sample XML
6. Review metadata extraction results
7. Verify transformed JSON structure
